  "validation": "Needs testing",
  "verification": "Exact installed-byte emulator verification covers native caller returns, actual timing episodes, corrected fixed-IPW envelope, interrupt publication, migration and native protections. Bench and on-car validation remain required.",
  "title": "Ignition Cut",
  "user_description": "Independent ignition-cut limiter with RPM hysteresis, optional fixed injector pulse width and an optional fixed ignition angle in a configurable RPM region below the cut limit. Provides shared timing and combustion-observation recovery for Launch Control V18.",
  "description": "MS41.1 Ignition Cut V18 retains V16 runtime ownership and calibrations. The active limiter angle is the later of the requested absolute angle and native protected timing. Native input and knock-sensor faults retain their veto; learned knock corrections are never cleared. Knock learning waits after actual spark cuts or timing changes through native window/reply/sample recovery using D805-D80B. Fixed IPW remains a base width with native cylinder and battery compensation; invalid or excessive corrected durations fall back to native fueling using the current synchronized segment envelope. D80C reports native, fixed base, or native fallback. Exact compatible predecessor pairs migrate together and retain configured calibration bytes.",
  "target": "MS41.1",
